# virsh — real-world examples

CLI for managing libvirt/KVM guests. On Tumbleweed: `sudo zypper in libvirt
virt-install`, then `sudo systemctl enable --now libvirtd`.

## Connect and list

```sh
virsh help

# Connect to a hypervisor
virsh connect qemu:///system

# Manage the homelab hypervisor remotely over ssh
virsh -c qemu+ssh://david@homelab/system list --all

# List domains
virsh list           # running only
virsh list --all     # all defined guests
```

## Control instances

```sh
virsh start <instance>
virsh shutdown <instance>     # graceful ACPI shutdown
virsh destroy <instance>      # hard power-off (not delete!)
virsh suspend <instance>
virsh resume <instance>

# Autostart a guest when libvirtd comes up (e.g. a pihole VM)
virsh autostart <instance>
virsh autostart --disable <instance>
```

## Save/restore state

```sh
virsh save <instance> /tmp/vm     # save memory state to file and stop
virsh restore /tmp/vm             # resume from the saved file

# Attach to the guest's serial console (exit with Ctrl+])
virsh console <instance>
```

## Define and edit instances

```sh
# Dump a guest's XML definition — also a handy backup
virsh dumpxml <instance> > dump.xml

virsh create dump.xml      # start a transient guest from XML
virsh define dump.xml      # register a persistent guest from XML
virsh edit <instance>      # edit XML in $EDITOR with validation
virsh undefine <instance>  # remove definition (disk images remain)

# Grow a guest disk while running
virsh blockresize <instance> --path vda --size 100G
```

## Info and snapshots

```sh
virsh dominfo <instance>
virsh vcpuinfo <instance>
virsh nodeinfo

# Snapshot before risky guest changes, roll back if it goes sideways
virsh snapshot-create-as <instance> pre-upgrade
virsh snapshot-list <instance>
virsh snapshot-revert <instance> pre-upgrade

virsh ttyconsole <instance>
virsh quit    # leave interactive CLI
```

## Command reference

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `list --all` | show all guests |
| `start` / `shutdown` / `destroy` | power management |
| `autostart` | start guest at host boot |
| `dumpxml` / `define` / `edit` | manage XML definitions |
| `console` | serial console (Ctrl+] to exit) |
| `snapshot-create-as` / `snapshot-revert` | snapshots |
| `dominfo` / `nodeinfo` | guest / host info |
